WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:02.120
The perfect childhood.

00:00:02.120 --> 00:00:03.399
School is out.

00:00:03.399 --> 00:00:04.399
Shoes are off.

00:00:04.399 --> 00:00:09.750
You’re sprinting across the hot, sandy beach,
smiling for no apparent reason; because back

00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:12.349
then you didn’t even need one.

00:00:12.349 --> 00:00:15.010
Did I mention there’s an orange cone on
your head?

00:00:15.010 --> 00:00:16.539
Where’d it come from?

00:00:16.539 --> 00:00:17.789
Why is it there?

00:00:17.789 --> 00:00:19.619
What is the point?

00:00:19.619 --> 00:00:21.619
Do not think too deeply about it.

00:00:21.619 --> 00:00:24.250
There is no room for symbolism in the summer.

00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:27.930
There is no use overanalyzing the antics of
teenage youth.

00:00:27.930 --> 00:00:33.800
It’s just a cone; and you are just a kid,
doing things for no other reason than that

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.100
you want to.

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:36.570
You’re busy living.

00:00:36.570 --> 00:00:37.920
Doing your thing.

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:40.510
Responsibility is still years away.

00:00:40.510 --> 00:00:43.000
Such a pretty picture we’re painting, isn’t
it?

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:49.100
But this is SCP Explained, so of course, by
now, you’ve figured out this is all a misdirection,

00:00:49.100 --> 00:00:50.100
didn’t you?

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:52.220
Well, here it comes.

00:00:52.220 --> 00:00:53.220
Watch closely.

00:00:53.220 --> 00:00:54.960
Look at you run.

00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:58.239
Moving toward nothing as if it means everything.

00:00:58.239 --> 00:01:02.310
Look at that smile, the wind whipping through
the gap in your teeth.

00:01:02.310 --> 00:01:03.310
Soak it in.

00:01:03.310 --> 00:01:06.840
In twenty years, your face muscles will have
forgotten the movement.

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:08.369
Look at you live!

00:01:08.369 --> 00:01:11.509
Yes, go on, soak it in.

00:01:11.509 --> 00:01:17.250
You will be chasing this feeling your whole
life while moving further and further away

00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:18.250
from it.

00:01:18.250 --> 00:01:19.250
Oof.

00:01:19.250 --> 00:01:20.390
Depressing, isn’t it?

00:01:20.390 --> 00:01:21.759
We think so too.

00:01:21.759 --> 00:01:26.330
But here is the silver lining, something you’d
be wise to celebrate…

00:01:26.330 --> 00:01:29.270
At least you have this moment to look back
on.

00:01:29.270 --> 00:01:31.899
The memory is with you forever.

00:01:31.899 --> 00:01:34.060
Not everyone is so lucky.

00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:36.880
Not everyone has a good childhood.

00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:40.669
Furthermore, not everyone even has a childhood
at all.

00:01:40.669 --> 00:01:43.770
Some live beyond the expectations of age.

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:46.520
Imagine a fourteen-year-old forced to be forty.

00:01:46.520 --> 00:01:49.909
That is not to say they have to pay taxes
or can run for senate.

00:01:49.909 --> 00:01:50.909
No.

00:01:50.909 --> 00:01:55.770
This level of forced maturity that I'm speaking
of transcends the scope of average adulthood.

00:01:55.770 --> 00:02:01.459
So, let’s not imagine a kid going through
the mundane life of a cubicle junkie: filing

00:02:01.459 --> 00:02:04.960
papers, pretending to work, and answering
phone calls.

00:02:04.960 --> 00:02:07.639
Instead, let’s do this.

00:02:07.639 --> 00:02:10.119
Imagine a kid going to war.

00:02:10.119 --> 00:02:13.579
Imagine a kid carrying out stealth assassination
missions.

00:02:13.579 --> 00:02:18.970
Imagine a kid being locked in containment
living with little human interaction and freedom.

00:02:18.970 --> 00:02:24.239
This is all to say, imagine a kid…not being
a kid at all.

00:02:24.239 --> 00:02:27.860
Now, this is more like an SCP Explained.

00:02:27.860 --> 00:02:32.730
This is the sad story of someone who had to
say goodbye to the joys of adolescence earlier

00:02:32.730 --> 00:02:34.769
than anyone ever should have to.

00:02:34.769 --> 00:02:38.090
In fact, they didn’t even get to say goodbye
at all.

00:02:38.090 --> 00:02:41.060
This is the story of SCP-105.

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:47.500
Now, to be clear, SCP–105 is not a blood-thirsty
demon living in the shadows.

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:52.680
It is not an un-squishable spider dancing
across your hardwood floor, mocking the soles

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:55.079
of your shoes as they stomp down with no success.

00:02:55.079 --> 00:03:01.409
It is not a grand piano in a hotel lobby absorbing
the DNA of all who touch its keys.

00:03:01.409 --> 00:03:06.060
And it is not a freezer that tempts late-night
snackers to reach deeper and deeper toward

00:03:06.060 --> 00:03:11.980
an ever-elusive hot fudge sundae until they
are sucked in, frozen solid, sold for millions,

00:03:11.980 --> 00:03:16.780
and displayed as decorative ice sculptures
atop the center of punch bowls at parties

00:03:16.780 --> 00:03:18.069
for rich politicians.

00:03:18.069 --> 00:03:19.069
No.

00:03:19.069 --> 00:03:22.950
We’ll just have to get to those on a different
day.

00:03:22.950 --> 00:03:28.260
Because SCP-105 is just… how do I put this…
a girl.

00:03:28.260 --> 00:03:31.099
Yes, a small, unremarkable-looking girl.

00:03:31.099 --> 00:03:36.660
At the time of acquisition, she was just 1.54
meters tall and weighed 50kg.

00:03:36.660 --> 00:03:40.629
Even those of you listening with little to
no instinctual senses for converting meters

00:03:40.629 --> 00:03:45.390
and kilograms to feet and pounds can still
understand this is no frightful giant we’re

00:03:45.390 --> 00:03:46.540
talking about.

00:03:46.540 --> 00:03:50.739
Lining up a class by height, she’d blend
in somewhere toward the middle.

00:03:50.739 --> 00:03:54.969
And if you look even closer, beyond the shallow
surface of measurements and toward the details

00:03:54.969 --> 00:04:00.560
of her face, even still, you won’t find
a single freckle to fear.

00:04:00.560 --> 00:04:04.200
SCP-105 has blue eyes and blonde hair.

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:08.639
Nothing coastal Californians haven’t seen
a million times over just this Monday.

00:04:08.639 --> 00:04:13.950
Formally known as Iris Thompson, SCP-105 has
no discernable oddities.

00:04:13.950 --> 00:04:17.169
If you saw her jumping rope, you wouldn’t
point and stare.

00:04:17.169 --> 00:04:20.750
If you saw her at the park playing with your
children, you wouldn’t pull them away and

00:04:20.750 --> 00:04:22.210
squeeze them tight.

00:04:22.210 --> 00:04:26.360
If you saw her walking toward you on the sidewalk,
you wouldn’t turn around and run away in

00:04:26.360 --> 00:04:27.720
the other direction.

00:04:27.720 --> 00:04:31.640
By herself, SCP-105 is not too different from
anyone else.

00:04:31.640 --> 00:04:37.240
No matter how close we zoom in on her appearance,
personality, or her tendencies there is nothing

00:04:37.240 --> 00:04:39.250
to see that triggers alarms.

00:04:39.250 --> 00:04:41.990
If you ask her to spit fire, she won’t.

00:04:41.990 --> 00:04:45.919
If you conduct a lab experiment where she
has to find the exit of a maze using only

00:04:45.919 --> 00:04:49.050
her sense of smell, she will get lost and
fail.

00:04:49.050 --> 00:04:54.229
This is all to say, if you look too closely
through the microscope at SCP-105, you might

00:04:54.229 --> 00:04:55.949
miss her anomalous abilities.

00:04:55.949 --> 00:05:01.620
Instead, you’d be better off taking a step
back and just watching her live her life.

00:05:01.620 --> 00:05:05.990
And that is all that she wanted to do: live
her life.

00:05:05.990 --> 00:05:08.020
Is that so much to ask?

00:05:08.020 --> 00:05:11.500
The first thing you will notice is that she
isn’t alone.

00:05:11.500 --> 00:05:16.710
And like in any good buddy-buddy film, her
counterpart reveals more to her character.

00:05:16.710 --> 00:05:18.930
So who is standing by her side?

00:05:18.930 --> 00:05:24.020
Who is the co-star of this film that pushes
our protagonist into The Foundation’s spotlight?

00:05:24.020 --> 00:05:26.110
Well, it’s no person at all.

00:05:26.110 --> 00:05:29.470
It’s a camera, her camera.

00:05:29.470 --> 00:05:35.940
SCP-105-B is a Polaroid One Step Express,
manufactured in 1982.

00:05:35.940 --> 00:05:40.650
It does not appear to have any out-of-the-ordinary
physical characteristics and appears to be,

00:05:40.650 --> 00:05:46.729
for all intents and purposes, a normal Polaroid
camera, operating as expected for all persons

00:05:46.729 --> 00:05:49.740
aside from SCP-105.

00:05:49.740 --> 00:05:53.319
When you point it at a subject, they don’t
get sucked into the lens.

00:05:53.319 --> 00:05:56.000
The flash can’t blind an army of soldiers.

00:05:56.000 --> 00:05:59.280
When you say cheese, it doesn’t shoot out
a brick of cheddar.

00:05:59.280 --> 00:06:01.480
The camera is nothing more than a camera.

00:06:01.480 --> 00:06:05.039
That is, until in the hands of Iris Thompson.

00:06:05.039 --> 00:06:09.400
What’s more unique than the camera itself
are the photographs it produces.

00:06:09.400 --> 00:06:17.270
When SCP-105 holds a photograph taken by SCP-105-B,
the picture changes from a still shot to that

00:06:17.270 --> 00:06:22.310
of a real-time image of the person, location,
or object photographed.

00:06:22.310 --> 00:06:26.550
Regardless of the subject of the photograph,
the image will convert itself into what appears

00:06:26.550 --> 00:06:30.580
to be a handheld Livestream of whatever was
pictured.

00:06:30.580 --> 00:06:32.840
Imagine a photograph of a waterfall.

00:06:32.840 --> 00:06:38.759
If held by SCP-105, you do not just see the
image of a waterfall, but you will physically

00:06:38.759 --> 00:06:43.120
see the water falling, splashing down onto
the rocks below.

00:06:43.120 --> 00:06:48.280
It is similar to holding your cell phone and
watching a GIF, however, instead of just watching,

00:06:48.280 --> 00:06:53.860
Iris is able to interact with it in a way
beyond any technology has ever allowed.

00:06:53.860 --> 00:06:59.770
SCP-105 is then able to move her arm through
and into the photograph and manipulate objects

00:06:59.770 --> 00:07:04.310
within reach of the original point at which
the photograph was first taken.

00:07:04.310 --> 00:07:06.960
Yes, you heard me right.

00:07:06.960 --> 00:07:13.220
SCP-105-2 doesn’t just offer Iris quick
prints of memories…it gives her much more,

00:07:13.220 --> 00:07:16.560
granting her access to a new dimension.

00:07:16.560 --> 00:07:20.960
Although this is clearly a unique situation
for Iris, it doesn’t mean that Iris is the

00:07:20.960 --> 00:07:23.449
only one affected by this anomaly.

00:07:23.449 --> 00:07:28.539
When she engages with the photographs, it
actually affects the world attached to them.

00:07:28.539 --> 00:07:32.849
That is to say, there are consequences to
her actions.

00:07:32.849 --> 00:07:38.620
Every photograph she has ever taken is essentially
a portal to a world of problems.

00:07:38.620 --> 00:07:42.900
Witnesses who have been on the other side
of the photograph while SCP-105 was manipulating

00:07:42.900 --> 00:07:48.110
it, report seeing her hand reaching out from
an invisible portal and carrying whatever

00:07:48.110 --> 00:07:50.139
actions she pleases.

00:07:50.139 --> 00:07:54.759
Once her arm is inside the photograph, she
has the freedom to control the image as she

00:07:54.759 --> 00:07:55.759
wishes.

00:07:55.759 --> 00:07:58.689
This ability has obvious benefits for anyone.

00:07:58.689 --> 00:08:02.129
Imagine being able to carry around with you
a photograph of your oven.

00:08:02.129 --> 00:08:06.539
Then, whenever you get that paranoid feeling
that you forgot to turn it off, you can reach

00:08:06.539 --> 00:08:09.930
into the polaroid and turn the dial how you
please.

00:08:09.930 --> 00:08:14.629
But the peace of mind is just a small benefit
of this power, and it’s easy to assume that

00:08:14.629 --> 00:08:19.409
anyone would be tempted to use their abilities
for far more than just controlling at-home

00:08:19.409 --> 00:08:22.110
kitchen appliances while on vacation.

00:08:22.110 --> 00:08:27.740
The Foundation, specifically, concerns itself
with bigger, more ambitious uses of anomalous

00:08:27.740 --> 00:08:28.740
power.

00:08:28.740 --> 00:08:31.680
And the power, in this case, wasn’t just
in the camera.

00:08:31.680 --> 00:08:37.230
While 105-B helps Iris use her powers most
efficiently, she is still able to manipulate

00:08:37.230 --> 00:08:42.730
objects through photographs taken by other
cameras, though not quite as well as when

00:08:42.730 --> 00:08:45.160
she’s using her favorite camera.

00:08:45.160 --> 00:08:50.290
Noting that 105-B and the photographs taken
by said camera have no unusual properties

00:08:50.290 --> 00:08:56.810
when used by any other person except for SCP-105,
it was clear to The Foundation who the greater

00:08:56.810 --> 00:08:59.950
anomaly in the situation really was.

00:08:59.950 --> 00:09:04.330
The tool wasn’t of their interest, but rather
the person wielding it.

00:09:04.330 --> 00:09:07.040
But how did this all come to their attention?

00:09:07.040 --> 00:09:10.880
Is The Foundation really investigating the
life of a girl playing with a camera in her

00:09:10.880 --> 00:09:11.880
bedroom?

00:09:11.880 --> 00:09:15.710
Well, some moments are just too big to be
bound by privacy.

00:09:15.710 --> 00:09:20.600
SCP-105 was brought to the forefront of The
Foundation's attention shortly after the murder

00:09:20.600 --> 00:09:22.170
of her boyfriend.

00:09:22.170 --> 00:09:26.550
Promptly after his death, the police investigated
the scene and looked for answers.

00:09:26.550 --> 00:09:30.160
And when looking for answers, they started
conjuring up questions.

00:09:30.160 --> 00:09:32.880
One of which put Iris at the center of their
search.

00:09:32.880 --> 00:09:34.580
“Where were you?”

00:09:34.580 --> 00:09:36.980
Her response wasn’t so straightforward.

00:09:36.980 --> 00:09:39.710
She wasn’t there, but then she was.

00:09:39.710 --> 00:09:42.720
The police pressed further, not understanding.

00:09:42.720 --> 00:09:47.590
SCP-105 explained that she was at home, but
once she learned of his death, she hurried

00:09:47.590 --> 00:09:48.850
over to him.

00:09:48.850 --> 00:09:53.120
This left the police even more suspicious,
as there was no way she could have been informed

00:09:53.120 --> 00:09:55.520
of the murder by an outside source.

00:09:55.520 --> 00:09:58.150
She must have been there all along.

00:09:58.150 --> 00:10:03.640
Seeing the skepticism in their faces, SCP-105
scrambled for an explanation.

00:10:03.640 --> 00:10:06.450
She took a deep breath and got her story straight.

00:10:06.450 --> 00:10:10.410
She claimed to have been on the phone with
her boyfriend at the time of the violent attack,

00:10:10.410 --> 00:10:15.120
and once she heard the commotion, it prompted
her to hurry over to his location, where she

00:10:15.120 --> 00:10:16.530
saw him dead.

00:10:16.530 --> 00:10:20.940
This excuse made logical sense, and so the
police dropped their suspicion.

00:10:20.940 --> 00:10:23.640
After all, Iris was just a small, innocent
teenager.

00:10:23.640 --> 00:10:28.810
However, just as quickly as the police moved
on from Iris, they returned to her, this time

00:10:28.810 --> 00:10:31.080
with tangible proof of their doubts.

00:10:31.080 --> 00:10:34.200
The telephone records did not correspond to
her story.

00:10:34.200 --> 00:10:36.940
She was never on the phone with her boyfriend
that night.

00:10:36.940 --> 00:10:40.420
It was then that SCP-105 had to confess.

00:10:40.420 --> 00:10:43.850
She informed her lawyer that she had, in fact,
been there for the murder.

00:10:43.850 --> 00:10:47.410
Well, not there… but… kinda there.

00:10:47.410 --> 00:10:50.810
She explained how she witnessed the murder
through a photograph she had taken with her

00:10:50.810 --> 00:10:52.530
boyfriend several days prior.

00:10:52.530 --> 00:10:56.910
The attorney in question disregarded the story
and recommended that the subject plead guilty.

00:10:56.910 --> 00:10:59.640
Iris, however, refused to do so.

00:10:59.640 --> 00:11:03.960
She was sticking to her truth, no matter how
crazy it made her seem.

00:11:03.960 --> 00:11:06.000
She went forward and told her story in court.

00:11:06.000 --> 00:11:07.800
It was met with derision.

00:11:07.800 --> 00:11:12.610
The judge and the jury didn’t even entertain
the possibility of any of it being true.

00:11:12.610 --> 00:11:14.040
Iris was flustered.

00:11:14.040 --> 00:11:18.770
She was a young teenage girl fighting for
her freedom, her only weapon being the truth.

00:11:18.770 --> 00:11:21.220
But the room wasn’t participating in her
reality.

00:11:21.220 --> 00:11:23.580
They dismissed her as crazy.

00:11:23.580 --> 00:11:27.850
And so when Iris offered to demonstrate her
ability, it was the last straw.

00:11:27.850 --> 00:11:31.560
The judge wouldn’t allow Iris to waste any
more of anyone’s time.

00:11:31.560 --> 00:11:33.980
She was sentenced to a psychiatric ward.

00:11:33.980 --> 00:11:36.210
Iris was determined to get out of there.

00:11:36.210 --> 00:11:38.180
She knew she didn’t belong.

00:11:38.180 --> 00:11:41.980
Luckily, someone else knew, too, that she
didn’t belong.

00:11:41.980 --> 00:11:45.520
And because of this, in a matter of days she
was out of there.

00:11:45.520 --> 00:11:47.250
But home wasn’t where she was heading.

00:11:47.250 --> 00:11:48.250
No.

00:11:48.250 --> 00:11:52.190
It wasn’t mom and dad picking her up from
the psychiatric ward, but rather the Foundation

00:11:52.190 --> 00:11:57.300
breaking her out, stealing her for themselves,
and bringing her to site-17.

00:11:57.300 --> 00:12:02.790
There at site-17, Foundation Personnel began
their mission, which started with trying to

00:12:02.790 --> 00:12:06.390
convince SCP-105 that they were on her side.

00:12:06.390 --> 00:12:14.130
They began by retrieving SCP-105-B from SCP-105's
home and replacing it with an identical model,

00:12:14.130 --> 00:12:17.550
only then to give it to her under the lie
that it was the original.

00:12:17.550 --> 00:12:19.710
The lies wouldn’t stop just there.

00:12:19.710 --> 00:12:24.510
They’d continue to pour over her reality
until it was impossible for her to recognize

00:12:24.510 --> 00:12:26.270
one from the other.

00:12:26.270 --> 00:12:30.580
SCP-105's parents were informed that she was
killed during the botched escape of another

00:12:30.580 --> 00:12:34.960
patient while both were in the custody of
a psychiatric care facility.

00:12:34.960 --> 00:12:39.690
In truth though, the Foundation wants nothing
more than to keep SCP-105 alive.

00:12:39.690 --> 00:12:43.560
However, they are not concerned about the
quality of her living.

00:12:43.560 --> 00:12:46.110
Iris was a tool for The Foundation.

00:12:46.110 --> 00:12:47.460
She was an asset.

00:12:47.460 --> 00:12:49.380
She was a secret weapon.

00:12:49.380 --> 00:12:54.950
She had powers they could have only dreamed
of, only now they existed.

00:12:54.950 --> 00:13:00.080
But before shooting their new shiny weapon,
they needed to learn how to use it properly.

00:13:00.080 --> 00:13:01.540
But with what manual?

00:13:01.540 --> 00:13:03.990
How do you learn how to use another human?

00:13:03.990 --> 00:13:08.570
Well, having seen enough Marvel movies, they
knew they would be better equipped with knowledge

00:13:08.570 --> 00:13:11.500
if they understood her origin story.

00:13:11.500 --> 00:13:17.300
So they began questioning Iris, trying to
get to the root cause of her anomalous aptitude.

00:13:17.300 --> 00:13:18.910
She was either ten or eleven.

00:13:18.910 --> 00:13:23.070
She remembers because she was looking at a
picture of the ocean, and she noticed that

00:13:23.070 --> 00:13:24.790
the waves began moving.

00:13:24.790 --> 00:13:28.490
Her parents said that she just had an overactive
imagination.

00:13:28.490 --> 00:13:33.230
When she first was able to move objects in
the photos, she was eleven, twelve, maybe.

00:13:33.230 --> 00:13:35.920
Her family took a trip to the Grand Canyon.

00:13:35.920 --> 00:13:39.810
She looked through the photo album after they
got home, and she brushed her hand up against

00:13:39.810 --> 00:13:40.860
one by accident.

00:13:40.860 --> 00:13:46.070
When she did, she pushed a rock over the edge,
falling into the canyon; she could actually

00:13:46.070 --> 00:13:48.370
hear it clatter on the way down.

00:13:48.370 --> 00:13:51.260
She became fascinated with photography after
that.

00:13:51.260 --> 00:13:55.470
Most of the time, it didn't work with photographs
she took, but her parents got her a Polaroid

00:13:55.470 --> 00:14:00.140
One Step Express camera that she’d been
begging them for since Christmas.

00:14:00.140 --> 00:14:04.090
After she got the camera, the photos got easier
to interact with.

00:14:04.090 --> 00:14:06.830
After hearing her story, the researcher made
her an offer.

00:14:06.830 --> 00:14:11.830
She’d be allowed certain freedoms if she
agreed to use her powers to do them a few

00:14:11.830 --> 00:14:13.030
favors.

00:14:13.030 --> 00:14:18.470
She could, at least in some capacity, act
her age, socialize, and do things a girl her

00:14:18.470 --> 00:14:20.280
grade would normally do.

00:14:20.280 --> 00:14:26.770
But in exchange, she had to first do things
that nobody any age should ever have to do.

00:14:26.770 --> 00:14:27.770
Iris agreed.

00:14:27.770 --> 00:14:32.800
And it was in this agreement that we see just
how desperate she was during her childhood.

00:14:32.800 --> 00:14:37.640
She was willing to risk everything for something
as small as a quick conversation with a guard,

00:14:37.640 --> 00:14:42.560
five minutes of jump rope, or simply a few
minutes spent under the sun.

00:14:42.560 --> 00:14:46.750
She was assigned to be a part of Mobile Task
Force Omega-7 to carry out a wide range of

00:14:46.750 --> 00:14:47.750
missions.

00:14:47.750 --> 00:14:52.040
And if the fate of the first humanoid SCP
recruited to Mobile Task Force Omega-7 was

00:14:52.040 --> 00:14:56.160
any indication of how this might play out,
Iris was in a lot of trouble.

00:14:56.160 --> 00:14:58.980
The Pandora's Box initiative had a history
of failure.

00:14:58.980 --> 00:15:04.550
Their previous efforts under "Team Able" ended
in the death of absolutely everyone.

00:15:04.550 --> 00:15:08.530
However, “Team Iris” began on a more hopeful
note.

00:15:08.530 --> 00:15:11.920
They carried out different missions than “Team
Able.”

00:15:11.920 --> 00:15:16.500
Instead of violent attacks, their primary
missions were reconnaissance and intelligence

00:15:16.500 --> 00:15:17.500
gathering.

00:15:17.500 --> 00:15:21.370
However, just because there were no swords
and blood drawn, the missions were not so

00:15:21.370 --> 00:15:22.370
harmless.

00:15:22.370 --> 00:15:26.810
Despite "Team Iris" carrying out over twenty
jobs in cooperation with the Bowe Commission,

00:15:26.810 --> 00:15:31.370
swiftly and without incident, their streak
eventually had to come to an end.

00:15:31.370 --> 00:15:36.460
The first disciplinary incident for SCP-105
involved the escalation of Team Iris missions

00:15:36.460 --> 00:15:38.440
from reconnaissance to assassinations.

00:15:38.440 --> 00:15:45.130
Yes, this teenage girl with not a violent
bone in her body was tasked to kill.

00:15:45.130 --> 00:15:48.300
Note that her only power is that of manipulating
photos.

00:15:48.300 --> 00:15:51.550
In her mind, this is nothing more than a party
trick.

00:15:51.550 --> 00:15:56.621
It was a gift she was born with, and she was
always aware that it was unique, but never

00:15:56.621 --> 00:15:58.840
did she expect it to be a curse.

00:15:58.840 --> 00:16:02.680
She liked being able to straighten books in
photographs of libraries.

00:16:02.680 --> 00:16:07.020
She liked being able to reach into photos
and hug her teddy bear that she no longer

00:16:07.020 --> 00:16:08.020
has.

00:16:08.020 --> 00:16:13.650
She liked being able to help, heal, and embrace
history…not alter it.

00:16:13.650 --> 00:16:18.300
SCP-105 violently opposed the use of her abilities
to carry out assassinations.

00:16:18.300 --> 00:16:23.600
They wanted her to murder people, and like
any girl of her nature would, she resisted.

00:16:23.600 --> 00:16:24.830
But they kept pressing.

00:16:24.830 --> 00:16:28.790
While some teenage girls are pressured by
parents to play sports they don’t particularly

00:16:28.790 --> 00:16:32.100
care for, this one was pressured to kill.

00:16:32.100 --> 00:16:37.270
During these events, SCP-105 became emotionally
distressed and attempted to deceive Foundation

00:16:37.270 --> 00:16:40.630
personnel into believing that her anomalous
traits had disappeared.

00:16:40.630 --> 00:16:43.660
She claimed she couldn’t carry out the missions
anymore.

00:16:43.660 --> 00:16:50.050
Her doctor submitted a report recommending
that SCP-105 be re-classified as Neutralized,

00:16:50.050 --> 00:16:54.890
undergo amnestic treatment, and be released
to the public with regular monitoring.

00:16:54.890 --> 00:17:00.370
After further investigation, The Foundation
realized the doctor was prioritizing SCP-105’s

00:17:00.370 --> 00:17:03.180
emotional state over the goals of The Foundation.

00:17:03.180 --> 00:17:04.410
They had built a friendship.

00:17:04.410 --> 00:17:08.279
He was the one telling her to pretend not
to have powers anymore.

00:17:08.279 --> 00:17:09.740
This was all found out.

00:17:09.740 --> 00:17:13.689
Thus, his recommendation to release Iris was
denied.

00:17:13.689 --> 00:17:18.589
With nothing to lose at that point, the doctor
even helped Iris try to escape The Foundation’s

00:17:18.589 --> 00:17:19.589
custody.

00:17:19.589 --> 00:17:20.589
But this failed.

00:17:20.589 --> 00:17:22.829
She was captured and the doctor was promptly
discharged.

00:17:22.829 --> 00:17:27.730
At that point, Iris had to start over again
to regain the trust of The Foundation.

00:17:27.730 --> 00:17:32.471
In yet another compromise, she re-demonstrated
her anomalous abilities in exchange for the

00:17:32.471 --> 00:17:37.620
restoration of limited privileges: nothing
more than occasionally being allowed to jump

00:17:37.620 --> 00:17:42.490
rope, getting a lollipop every Thursday, and
being informed of the recent trends on Tik

00:17:42.490 --> 00:17:43.490
Tok.

00:17:43.490 --> 00:17:46.120
And so this is where we know her to be.

00:17:46.120 --> 00:17:50.940
Continuously making sacrifices in exchange
for tiny teaspoons of teenage life.

00:17:50.940 --> 00:17:56.820
All the while she is growing older and older,
unfulfilled by the years she passes.

00:17:56.820 --> 00:18:01.460
And so while it is easy to look back on our
childhood with lust and longing, at least

00:18:01.460 --> 00:18:07.769
it was there, and is still there now, safely
stored in our memory, stored in the protection

00:18:07.769 --> 00:18:08.919
of the past.

00:18:08.919 --> 00:18:11.050
For Iris, this is not so.

00:18:11.050 --> 00:18:14.159
Her childhood is both behind her and in front
of her.

00:18:14.159 --> 00:18:17.159
It is something she moved on from too quickly.

00:18:17.159 --> 00:18:20.230
And it is a future she fights for every day.

00:18:20.230 --> 00:18:25.840
Even when she is ninety-seven, gray, decrepit,
and on her deathbed, she will be sacrificing

00:18:25.840 --> 00:18:28.320
her freedoms to feel fifteen.

00:18:28.320 --> 00:18:33.019
And so we have to wonder, is SCP-105 a danger
to anyone at all?

00:18:33.019 --> 00:18:35.260
I leave you with a question.

00:18:35.260 --> 00:18:39.950
Are we more likely to be attacked by a dog…or
the master holding its leash?

00:18:39.950 --> 00:18:46.580
Now go check out “SCP-053 - Young Girl”
and “SCP-3082 - Neverland's Lost Boys and

00:18:46.580 --> 00:18:48.130
Girls” for more peculiar anomalous children!

